    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Casual-Academic-Register---Health-Sciences---Allied-Health_JR0000010261": {
      "title": "Casual Academic Register - Health Sciences & Allied Health",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-02-26\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real‑world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities.   With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register About the College of Nursing and Health Sciences    At the College of Nursing and Health Sciences, we aim to be an innovator in contemporary education producing a safer and more resilient health and social care workforce. Our mission is to improve lives and empower communities, enabling better health and caring in the world through an exceptional student learning experience. At the College, our research mission is about co-creating new knowledge which promotes wellbeing, and better care and support, to individuals and communities across the lifespan. We work proactively with industry partners and professional bodies leading to more employable and innovative graduates.   Casual Register Opportunities   Flinders University has several casual registers where people can express their interest in casual work, if and when opportunities become available. This particular register is for roles in Health Sciences and Allied Health. Work may be available in both undergraduate and postgraduate courses and could take place at our Bedford Park campus, one of our regional campuses (Riverland, Port Pirie, or Mount Gambier), or online from any location.   Selection Criteria You are currently registered, or can be registered, as an Allied Health practitioner with AHPRA (if required for your role). You have, or can get, a valid South Australian Working with Children Check. Passionate about teaching and enjoy helping the next generation of graduates learn and grow in your field. Strong communication and teamwork skills. Knowledge and/or experience with current trends in health sciences and allied health. Experience teaching in a university setting (desirable). A postgraduate qualification in health or a related field (desirable). How to Register Upload your current CV/Resume detailing your qualifications and experience You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resume Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Please note, only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. Further Information Pursuant to Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA) this position may be deemed prescribed. It is an inherent requirement of a prescribed position that the successful candidate maintains a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University Please contact recruitment@flinders.edu.au  should you have any queries regarding casual opportunities."
    },
