    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Research-Associate-in-Marine-Biology--Biofouling---Molecular-Ecology-_JR0000017701-1": {
      "title": "Research Associate in Marine Biology (Biofouling & Molecular Ecology)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Full-Time | Two-year contract Academic Level A | $90,930 - $110,197 pa Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description About the Role We are seeking an enthusiastic and highly motivated Research Associate to join the ARC Training Centre for Biofilm Research & Innovation (BRIC) and contribute to an exciting research project investigating biofouling communities in Australian waters. Working under the direction of the Chief Investigator and in collaboration with project and partner investigators, you will play a key role in designing, managing and delivering research activities for the project. In this position, your duties will include, but not be limited to: Leading research investigating the establishment of marine biofouling communities on artificial structures. Apply advanced molecular and bioinformatic techniques to assess the diversity, composition, and temporal dynamics of biofouling communities. Design, conduct and analyse experiments examining biofouling processes on marine infrastructure. Contribute to the development of research methodologies, experimental protocols, and sampling strategies to support project objectives. Work collaboratively with an interdisciplinary team of researchers and project partners, including government agencies and industry stakeholders. Interpret and communicate research findings through technical reports, scientific publications, presentations, and stakeholder engagement activities. Assist with project management activities, including planning, data management, reporting, and achievement of project milestones. This position is open to candidates with Australian working rights. Relocation support may be available for the successful candidate. About You You will be passionate about protecting Australia’s marine environments and advancing the sustainable management of its oceans and waterways. You will be a collaborative, proactive and motivated researcher with a strong interest in marine biofouling, molecular ecology or a related field, committed to delivering high-quality, impactful research. As well as completion (or near-completion) of a PhD in Marine Biology or Marine Genomics or Marine Microbiology or Bioinformatics, you should demonstrate; Research experience in biofouling, marine invasive species, marine microbial ecology, or related fields. Knowledge of marine organism identification and taxonomy, particularly in relation to biofouling communities. A growing research profile in marine microbial ecology, molecular ecology, metagenomics, or a closely related discipline, evidenced by publications and other research outputs. Experience applying molecular and microbiological techniques, including genomic and metagenomic approaches, to address ecological research questions. Expertise in bioinformatic analyses and the interpretation of complex biological and ecological datasets. Demonstrated skills in quantitative data analysis, including proficiency in R, Python, MATLAB, or equivalent software. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to work effectively both independently and collaboratively within multidisciplinary research teams.   About the ARC Training Centre for Biofilm Research and Innovation  We are the leading Australian research and training centre tackling biofilm-related challenges.   The ARC Training Centre for Biofilm Research and Innovation , led by Flinders University, is a 5 year, $7.8m research and training program, bringing together 5 universities, 10 industry partners and key industry and regulatory bodies to deliver innovative research and biofilm solutions to tackle important issues for the maritime and water industries.  Biofilms grow on all surfaces and environments, from catheters to drinking water pipes and ships. They are complex organisations of cells that grow on both living and inert surfaces and are both viscous and elastic in nature. They can be made up of a single species or comprise several species of different types of microorganisms, including those that pose a threat to either human health or our environment. Biofilm attachment and development cannot be prevented completely thus they cost billions each year to those attempting to eradicate them.    By working with industries to develop innovative solutions that meet their needs and alleviate their biofilm-related problems, the ARC Training Centre for Biofilm Research and Innovation aims to: transform biofouling management strategies for maritime platforms; train the next generation of interdisciplinary scientists and engineers; and to develop biofilm management strategies across the defence and water industries to address evolving regulatory stringency.  Life at Flinders They say know your place.  We say you've found it right here. Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we’ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we’ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them.   So,   why work at Flinders?   17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers  We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus  health care services ,  gym  and  childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia).   Prescribed Conditions for Employment Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University.   These include: Flinders University will require a current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. The successful candidate will be required to obtain a baseline Security Clearance.     How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document.  This should be no more than 3 pages, and address the Key Position Capabilities of the position description . For more information regarding this position, please contact the Recruitment team via email at For more information regarding this position, please contact the Recruitment team via email at For more information regarding this position, please contact the Recruitment team via email at recruitment@flinders.edu.au or phone (08) 8201 2383.   Applications to be submitted before 10:00 pm (ACDT) on Sunday, 25 October 2026. Please note, late applications and applications sent via agencies will not be accepted . At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 25 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
    },
    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Social-Media-Officer_JR0000017752": {
      "title": "Social Media Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nPart time\n\nPart-Time at 0.5 FTE | Fixed term (12 months)  Higher Education Officer Level 5 | $84,599 - $93,366 (pro-rata) Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country   View Position Description     This is a unique opportunity for someone who possess native-level written and spoken communication skills in Mandarin Chinese and advanced English communication skills to work with Flinders Marketing and Student Recruitment Team.   About the Role   Ready to create content that reaches and inspires future students across one of China's most popular social media platforms? As the Social Media Officer (Chinese Channels), you'll help grow Flinders University's presence in China through engaging content, online community building, and digital campaigns that connect with prospective students.   In this role, you will be responsible for: Creating and sharing engaging content across Chinese social media channels, with a strong focus on Xiaohongshu (RED). Building and maintaining active online communities by responding to audiences and encouraging engagement. Tracking social media performance and using insights to improve content and grow audiences. Collaborating with colleagues across the University to showcase student stories and support international student recruitment.   For more information on the key position responsibilities, please see the position description   This position makes a significant contribution to the University’s strategic plan, “Changing 10 million lives, Every One Matters” by 2035, by building awareness of Flinders University among prospective students in China through engaging social media content. The role supports Flinders’ commitment to being student-centred, fostering a vibrant culture through storytelling, and driving innovation through the effective use of digital and social media platforms.   About You   You are a creative and motivated social media professional who understands Chinese social media and what audiences enjoy seeing online. You can create great content, build engagement, and use data to improve results.   To succeed in this role, you will have: Experience creating high-quality social media content, including videos, photography and written posts. Strong understanding of Chinese social media platforms, particularly Xiaohongshu (RED), trends and audience interests. Native-level written and spoken communication skills in both Mandarin Chinese and English. Ability to review social media results, identifying opportunities for improvement and managing multiple tasks effectively.   About the Marketing and Student Recruitment team    The Marketing and Student Recruitment team is evolving in 2026 with exciting new opportunities at our vibrant Bedford Park campus and the cutting-edge Flinders City Campus. As we accelerate our growth ambitions, we are looking for skilled and motivated team members to help drive our marketing strategies and initiatives. If you are passionate about shaping impactful marketing campaigns, building the Flinders University brand, and contributing to the recruitment of future students, we want to hear from you.   Join us in a team that is focused on innovation, excellence, and delivering results that will position Flinders as a leader in higher education.    Life at Flinders      They say know your place.  We say you've found it right here.    Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next.    Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we’ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we’ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create.    Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them.     So,  why work at Flinders?   17% Superannuation + salary packaging options   Flexible working arrangements   Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our  Thriving@Flinders  staff wellbeing program  Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers    We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards.   Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus  health care services ,  gym  and  childcare centre  (Bedford Park, South Australia).   Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice      Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment   Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.  We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies.   Please see here for our  Reconciliation Action Plan     Please see here for our  Indigenous Workforce Strategy        Prescribed Conditions for Employment   Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University.  This includes: A current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role.     How to Apply and Information   You are required to submit a CV, along with a Cover Letter as a separate document, telling us a little about yourself, and why you feel you are suited to this role. Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University. If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise the contact in the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through  recruitment@flinders.edu.au  or call 08 8201 2383.  For more information regarding this position, please contact  Laura Logan   Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 25 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
    },
    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Procurement-Category-Manager_JR0000017110": {
      "title": "Procurement Category Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nPosition Details   Full-Time | Fixed term (15 months) HEO9 - $133,860 + 17% Super Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description    About the Role   The Procurement Category Manager at Flinders University is responsible for the procurement and contracting of specified major commodity groups across the University, or for specific high-risk procurement projects.  The role involves developing an in-depth understanding of the University stakeholder requirements including extensive consultation with user groups and leading cross functional teams to deliver exceptional procurement outcomes. This may include being responsible for the creation or review of some or all documentation related to the procurement process and ensuring that appropriate changes and updates are made to Flinders University systems as well as procedures and guidelines. Working in this impactful role will involve: Developing procurement strategies to meet the commercial imperative of the University as well as stakeholder requirements, incorporating overall market approach, proposed contract type, scope and length. Undertaking procurement processes to achieve strategic outcomes, including preparing Acquisition Plans, undertaking market approaches, evaluation and recommendations, and all Governance reporting. Establishing and leading cross functional teams of stakeholders and/or functional experts as appropriate to undertake processes, including evaluations.  Ensuring stakeholders are appropriately engaged and managed. Ensuring project management protocols are maintained, and that appropriate reporting occurs with regards to progress, risks and issues. Please note, due to the nature of the role, you will be required to work from the Bedford Park campus. About You   We are looking for a skilled and personable procurement professional with: Experience in the development of procurement documentation including approvals documentation and market approach documentation. Well developed commercial sense, including negotiation of contracts and the drafting of contracts High level oral, written and interpersonal communication skills including being an effective listener and negotiator, being able to ask clear questions about issues and requirements, and experience in writing quality reports and recommendations for complex and sensitive issues. Proficiency in the identification, development and implementation of procurement strategies for a range of category groups or specific projects Demonstrated experience of managing a complex end to end procurement process from identification of customer needs through to contract execution and contract handover. About Finance and Procurement Services  Finance and Procurement Services assist the University to achieve its goals by providing quality leadership, information, and financial services. The Finance and Procurement Services team undertakes monthly financial management reporting and forecasting, annual budgets and monitoring performance against these budgets, all regulatory financial reporting, monthly compliance, procurement contracting and functional areas of paying suppliers, receipting revenue and annual financial statements.  While this role is based at Bedford Park, we have team members located across all of Flinders sites. Life at Flinders We're transforming and investing in people and facilities to create contemporary, stimulating, and satisfying learning and work environments that reflect our core values of excellence, innovation, courage, and integrity. Flinders is refocusing its strategic priorities with the aim of elevating its performance to be a top ten Australian university, and amongst the top 1% in the world. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. So,  why work at Flinders? 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options   Our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders initiative  Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers    We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards.   Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus  health care services ,  gym  and  childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia).   Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment   Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.  We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies.  Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan    Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy   Prescribed Conditions for Employment A current Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check which is satisfactory to the University will be required by Flinders University before the successful applicant can commence in this position . A criminal record will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role.   How to Apply and Information   In addition to uploading your CV, please submit a separate Suitability Statement of no more than 3 pages, addressing the key position capabilities of the Position Description. For more information regarding this position, please contact Deborah Ashdown Applications will be considered as they are received. To avoid disappointment, we encourage applicants to submit their application as soon as possible, as we may close the advertisement early should a suitable candidate be identified. If you have previously applied for this position, there is no need to submit another application. Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 25 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
