    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Senior-Network-Services-Officer_JR0000017747": {
      "title": "Senior Network Services Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Full-Time | Continuing Higher Education Officer Level 6 | $94,456 - $100,710 Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description   About the Role We're looking for someone with a strong foundation in networking who is curious, adaptable, and enjoys being part of a team.   While experience is valued, attitude is paramount. We want someone who is keen to learn, willing to get involved across infrastructure and technology domains when needed, and comfortable rolling up their sleeves to solve problems wherever they arise. This role is ideal for someone who sees every challenge as an opportunity to learn, improve, and contribute.   The Network Engineer plays a key role in the delivery, support, and continuous improvement of the University's network infrastructure and connectivity services. Working within the Cloud & Infrastructure Services team, you will help maintain reliable, secure, and scalable network services that support teaching, learning, research, and business operations across the University.   This is a hands-on technical role that will suit an engineer who enjoys solving problems, working collaboratively, and contributing beyond their core area of expertise when required.   As the Senior Network Services Officer, you will be responsible for: Supporting the delivery, management and continuous improvement of the University's network services and infrastructure. Contributing to the implementation of network technology strategies, projects and roadmap initiatives. Partnering with stakeholders to provide technical expertise and enhance customer-focused network services. Identifying and mitigating risks, while monitoring emerging technologies and supporting best-practice network operations.   A more comprehensive list of duties is available from the Position Description   This position makes a significant contribution to the University’s strategic plan to “Changing 10 million lives, Every One Matters”, by 2035 through the delivery of secure, reliable and future-focused network services that enable teaching, research and operations across the University. The role supports a culture of innovation, continuous improvement and agile ways of working to meet evolving technology and business needs.   About You   To be successful in this role, you will demonstrate: Relevant qualifications in Information Technology (or a related discipline) and/or equivalent experience in a technical IT environment. Experience in one or more areas including routing protocols, network troubleshooting, switching architectures, network security, firewalls, VPNs or multi-vendor network environments. Strong analytical, planning and problem-solving skills, with the ability to identify and deliver effective technical solutions. Excellent communication and stakeholder engagement skills, coupled with experience working collaboratively in agile or matrix-based environments.   Experience within the higher education sector and/or Cisco networking environments, including CCNA certification or equivalent experience, will be highly regarded.   What We're Looking For   You are a technically capable network professional with strong analytical and problem-solving skills, a customer-focused approach and a genuine desire to continuously develop your expertise. You enjoy working collaboratively, building effective relationships with stakeholders and contributing to the delivery of reliable, high-quality technology services.   Why Join the Team?   We're building a team of people who are collaborative, adaptable, and willing to help wherever needed. While networking is the primary focus of this role, we are looking for someone who understands that delivering great technology outcomes is a team sport.   If you're the type of person who enjoys learning, isn't afraid to step outside your comfort zone, and wants exposure to a broad range of infrastructure technologies, we'd love to hear from you.   Technical skills can be learned. Curiosity, initiative, teamwork, and attitude are what make great engineers. Opportunity to work with modern cloud, network, and security technologies   What Success Looks Like   After 12 months in this role, you will have: Become a trusted member of the Infrastructure Services team. Built a strong understanding of the University's network and technology environment. Contributed to service improvements and infrastructure projects. Developed skills beyond traditional networking into cloud, security, and platform technologies. Established strong working relationships across IDS and the broader University.   This is an excellent opportunity for a network engineer who wants more than \"just networking\" and is looking to grow into a well-rounded infrastructure professional   Life at Flinders   They say know your place.  We say you've found it right here.  Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next.  Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we’ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we’ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create.  Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them.     Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment   Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.  We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies.   Please see here for our  Reconciliation Action Plan     Please see here for our  Indigenous Workforce Strategy       Prescribed Conditions for Employment   Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. This includes: A current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role.   How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement of no more than 3 pages, addressing the below Key Position Capabilities of the Position Description : Well-developed thinking, planning and analytical skills. Well-developed self-improvement and growth mindset/approach to the role and as part of a wider team. Well-developed interpersonal influence and demonstrated ability to negotiate and communicate effectively with staff and customers across a diverse organisation particularly during the design, management and implementation of customer solutions. Cisco Certified Network Associate (CCNA) certification or demonstrated experience in configuring or managing a CISCO Environment. Well-developed experience in at least one of current routing protocols, network troubleshooting techniques, a multi-vendor/multi-protocol environment, modern switching architectures, structured cabling standards and network security environments, including but not limited to firewalls and VPNs. Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University. If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise the contact in the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through recruitment@flinders.edu.au or call 08 8201 2383. For more information regarding this position, please contact Warren Pearse Certification National Police Certificate - Australian Federal Police Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 25 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
    },
    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/HDR-Engagement-Senior-Support-Officer_JR0000017724": {
      "title": "HDR Engagement Senior Support Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nPosition Details 5-Years Fixed Term I Full Time Higher Education Officer Level 6 I $94,456 - $100,710 + 17% Super Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description A Role with Impact: The HDR Engagement Senior Support Officer is a key role within the Office of Graduate Research (OGR), providing high-level administrative, project and stakeholder support for national and international Higher Degree by Research (HDR) engagement and partnership activities.   Working closely with the Dean of Graduate Research, HDR Strategic Operations and Quality Assurance Partner, College HDR Coordinators and the HDR Engagement and Partnerships Manager, you will support initiatives including cotutelle arrangements, industry internships, scholarships and the National Industry PhD Program. You will coordinate projects, reporting, committees and events while providing advice and support to HDR students, supervisors and internal and external stakeholders.   The HDR Engagement Senior Support Officer will: Support HDR engagement and partnership initiatives, including cotutelles, internships, industry scholarships and the National Industry PhD Program. Coordinate projects, reporting, committees and events that support national and international HDR engagement and partnership activities. Provide advice and high-quality support to HDR students, supervisors and stakeholders on relevant policies, procedures and engagement opportunities. Build strong relationships and contribute to continuous improvement, working across Colleges, professional services and external industry partners to enhance HDR engagement and services   About You You are an organised, collaborative and highly capable professional with experience providing administrative, project or coordination support, ideally within the higher education sector.   You bring strong attention to detail, excellent communication skills and the ability to manage multiple priorities while delivering high-quality outcomes. You are confident interpreting policies and procedures, working with a diverse range of stakeholders and providing professional advice and support in a complex environment.   You demonstrate: Experience providing high-level administrative, project or coordination support, preferably within higher education, research partnerships or industry engagement. The ability to interpret, apply and provide advice on complex policies, procedures and guidelines, with strong attention to detail and accuracy. Experience working with databases and complex information systems, together with strong Microsoft Office skills. An understanding of current issues affecting the higher education sector, particularly HDR engagement, research partnerships and industry collaboration.   About the Office of Graduate Research: The Office of Graduate Research (OGR) supports the success, development and impact of Flinders University’s Higher Degree by Research (HDR) community. Our experienced team provides expert support across the HDR lifecycle, from admissions, progression and examination through to research training, employability, industry engagement, international opportunities and supervisor development. We are committed to creating an exceptional HDR experience, fostering research excellence and connecting our researchers with opportunities to make a meaningful impact.   Life at Flinders They say know your place.  We say you've found it right here. Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. So,  why work at Flinders? 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our  Thriving@Flinders  staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers  We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus  health care services ,  gym  and  childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia). Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice  Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.  We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies. Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy Prescribed Conditions for Employment A current Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check which is satisfactory to the University will be required by Flinders University before the successful applicant can commence in this position. A criminal record will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role.   How to Apply and Information As well as a CV, you are required to submit a Suitability Statement of no more than 3 pages, addressing the below four Key Position Capabilities of the position description : Demonstrated ability to interpret, apply and provide advice on complex policies, procedures and guidelines. Strong attention to detail, accuracy, and demonstrated ability to deliver very high standards of work relating to research partnerships and/or industry engagement. Proficiency in working with a complex database such as a student management information system. Experience and/or a demonstrated understanding of the current issues impacting on the higher education sector, particularly as pertains to HDR engagement and partnership activities. For more information regarding this position, please contact Professor Lucy Lewis . Applications to be submitted before 10:00 pm (ACDT) on Sunday, 25 October 2026. Please note, late applications and applications sent via agencies will not be accepted . At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 25 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
    },
    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Senior-Risk-Audit-Specialist_JR0000017714": {
      "title": "Senior Risk and Audit Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Details   Full-Time | Continuing Higher Education Officer Level 8 | $116,349 - $128,806 Location:  Bedford Park / Kaurna Country   View Position Description   About the Role   We are seeking a highly capable Senior Risk and Audit Specialist to join Information and Digital Services (IDS) at Flinders University. Reporting to the Senior Information Security Audit & Risk Lead, you will play a key role in strengthening governance, risk and compliance practices across a complex and evolving digital environment.   Working closely with IDS leaders and stakeholders across the University, you will support the ongoing development and continuous improvement of risk and governance frameworks, policies and processes. You will provide expert guidance on risk, audit and compliance activities, contribute to governance reporting, and help ensure strategic and operational initiatives align with best practice governance standards. This is an excellent opportunity for a governance and risk professional who enjoys influencing outcomes, building strong relationships and driving continuous improvement within a collaborative and forward-thinking team.   Key responsibilities include: Supporting the development and continuous improvement of IDS governance and risk frameworks, policies, processes and standards. Providing advice, reporting and support to governance forums, leadership teams and stakeholders to strengthen risk, audit and compliance outcomes. Collaborating with IDS teams to ensure audit, risk and compliance activities align with operational priorities and strategic objectives. Contributing to the development and management of governance, risk, audit and compliance models that support informed decision-making and prioritisation. Undertaking secretariat responsibilities for key IDS governance committees and coordinating associated actions, communications and initiatives.   For a more comprehensive list of duties, please see the Position Description.   About You   You are an experienced governance, risk or audit professional who enjoys bringing structure, insight and continuous improvement to complex environments. You have a collaborative approach, strong stakeholder engagement skills and the ability to balance strategic thinking with operational delivery. You are motivated by the opportunity to influence positive outcomes and help strengthen governance and risk practices across a large and complex organisation.   To be successful in this role, you will demonstrate: Significant experience in governance, risk, audit or compliance roles within a complex environment. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to identify risks and deliver practical recommendations. Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to influence and build effective working relationships. Experience developing, implementing or supporting governance frameworks, risk management processes and reporting activities. Relevant postgraduate qualifications and/or an equivalent combination of education, training and professional experience.   About Information and Digital Services   Information and Digital Services (IDS) are a pivotal resource of the University, providing information and digital technology services and support to the Flinders University staff and student community. The IDS team apply technical expertise to support university projects and provide core services such as the IDS Service Desk, Audio visual, simulation and event services, Information security and identity access management services and more.   Life at Flinders   They say know your place.  We say you've found it right here.   Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next.    Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we’ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we’ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create.    Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them.     So,  why work at Flinders?   17% Superannuation + salary packaging options   Flexible working arrangements   Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our  Thriving@Flinders  staff wellbeing program  Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers    We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards.   Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus  health care services ,  gym  and  childcare centre  (Bedford Park, South Australia).   Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice   Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment      Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.  We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies.   Please see here for our  Reconciliation Action Plan     Please see here for our  Indigenous Workforce Strategy        Prescribed Conditions for Employment   Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. This includes: A current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role.     How to Apply and Information   You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document.  This should be no more than 3 pages, and address the Key Position Capabilities of the  position description Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University. If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise the contact in the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through  recruitment@flinders.edu.au  or call 08 8201 2383.  For more information regarding this position, please contact  Tristan Bibbo Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 20 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
